      "parent": {
        "id": "2034:25417",
        "type": "SECTION",
        "name": "Feedback/Alert"
      },
      "description": "PURPOSE: A prominent, inline message block communicating status directly within page content (not floating above it).\n\nWHEN TO USE: Persistent, contextual messages tied to the content on the page (a warning about a specific setting, a success confirmation after an action completes and stays visible).\n\nWHEN NOT TO USE: Transient, auto-dismissing notifications not tied to page content (use Toast instead, which floats and is typically temporary).\n\nACCESSIBILITY: Should render with role=\"alert\" (for Error/Warning, which need immediate announcement) or role=\"status\" (for Info/Success, less urgent) so screen readers announce it appropriately.\n\nCOMMON MISTAKES: Using Alert for something that should auto-dismiss (that's Toast's job) — Alert is meant to persist until the user or system explicitly removes it.\n\nTOKENS USED: color/info/100, color/success/100, color/warning/100, color/danger/100 (backgrounds), semantic/feedback/info/success/warning, semantic/action/danger (icon + accent), semantic/text/primary, semantic/text/secondary.\n\nPROPERTIES: Type (Info/Success/Warning/Error) as variants. Title (text), Description (text), Show close (boolean)."
    },
